===Alternative forms===
Note the regionally different forms of this character which are encoded separately in [[Unicode]]:
* {{lang|mul|戶}} (top stroke connects to left stroke, as found in the historical [[w:Kangxi dictionary|Kangxi dictionary]]) - used in Taiwan and South Korea.
* {{l|mul|戸}} (top stroke is a horizontal line that does not connect to other strokes) - used in Japan.
* {{l|mul|户}} (top stroke is a slanting dot) - used in mainland China, Hong Kong, Singapore and Malaysia.
Note also the different stroke order: {{l|mul|户}} and {{l|mul|戸}} have the leftmost {{l|mul|丿}} as the final (fourth) stroke, while {{lang|mul|戶}} (this character) has {{l|mul|丿}} as the second stroke.

