===Etymology 1===
This post-classical word (its earliest extant attestation is in {{w|Shuowen}}) was pronounced *''teŋ'' in Late Old Chinese, as would be expected from a {{zh-l|*丁}} phonetic. By the early {{w|Ming dynasty|Ming}} period, the character had been borrowed ({{zh-m|訓讀|tr=-}}) for another word with the same meaning but a different pronunciation, without the nasal ending. This may be related to the previous reading, as a dialectal variant. In Mandarin and some other varieties, the new reading became standard; however, derivations of the older pronunciation are still used in other varieties such as Wu and Min Nan, as well as Vietnamese ({{m|vi|đánh}}).

It has been compared to {{cog|lus|dêng||to throw; to fling; to hammer}} and proposed to be from {{der|zh|sit}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Also compare {{cog|mkh-pro|*dah|*dah ~ daʔ|to hit, to meet}}, whence {{cog|mnw|ဒး||tr=tɛ̀h|to hit (a mark), meet with, reach [goal], be correct, apposite, to fit}} and {{cog|km|ទះ||to slap, to strike}}.

The pronunciation ''da'' is recorded in {{lw|zh|六書故}} as {{lang|zh|都假[[切]]}}.

